      ],
      "source": "https://www.lakesnwoods.com/Mazeppa.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In its early years, Mazeppa was a flour‑milling center that produced 600 barrels a day and employed 80 workers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mazeppa%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s mill burned down on February 2, 1891, and foul play was suspected.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
